[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448244265,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448312224,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448317495,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448320557,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448323344,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448326008,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44832863,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448331072,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448333679,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448336116,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448338645,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448341282,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below 12 qubits (8 with mid-circuit measurement) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448345957,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches 12 qubits, or 8 with mid-circuit measurement (docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md, \"CPU against T4\") | IBM jobs; narrow replays, which the T4 speeds up by at most 3 times |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448349246,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448351955,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. An account without Persona identity verification gets a 4-core CPU machine for every TPU request; a verified account's request queues for a TPU, one batch session at a time (docs/notes/kaggle/tpu-research.md) | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448355038,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448358014,"data":"| A 15-qubit run (decision-gated) | the substrate an approved written case names: Kaggle T4 x2 or build host Aer, a GPU state wider than one T4 cache-blocked across both (`calibration_snapshot.blocking_options`; docs/notes/kaggle/gpu-runbook.md), or Tuna-17 through Quantum Inspire, whose `submit` refuses while another session's hardware job is live | any substrate the case does not name |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448361223,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 16 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448365432,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448368312,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448371305,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448373732,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448376265,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448378701,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448387137,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448390505,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448393172,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448395759,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448398362,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices, the Aer device the entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44840096,"data":"   runs on (`entry_aer_device`) and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448403527,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack, built and proved by\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448406208,"data":"   `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`. `--fetch` downloads the seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44840889,"data":"   archives `RELEASES` pins and keeps each only if its sha256 matches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448411549,"data":"   `--install` installs sixteen of them with `pip install --no-deps`,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448414221,"data":"   applying `BUILD_RECIPES` (the cayley-dickson, SplitOct and pyquaternion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448416826,"data":"   PKGBUILD `prepare()` steps) and taking the Octonion-Sedenion wheel as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448419681,"data":"   published, then installs `RUNTIME_PINS`: numpy-quaternion, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448422273,"data":"   seventeenth, as its pinned compiled wheel, and numba, sparse and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448424942,"data":"   anywidget. `--extract` binds all seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448427494,"data":"   installed distributions to their archives and regenerates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448430153,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json`; the kernel stops with exit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448432841,"data":"   code 3 unless those bytes equal the retained ones. The build host passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448435425,"data":"   the same test against its Arch packages, so a run that reaches its entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448437989,"data":"   used the same algebra code as the host. The file's `packages` field\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448440726,"data":"   records the versions `kernel_main.REPORTED_PACKAGES` names, nine of the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448443327,"data":"   seventeen algebra distributions; the byte comparison binds the rest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448445924,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448448529,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448451138,"data":"4. The entry's stdout and stderr, written to `stdout.txt` and `stderr.txt`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448453722,"data":"   as the entry prints (`kernel_main.start_entry` sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448456661,"data":"   `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`), then its exit code and the repository files it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448459317,"data":"   changed, which the kernel copies under `repo/` after the entry exits.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448462037,"data":"   A session Kaggle ends at `--timeout` still returns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448464603,"data":"   `/kaggle/working/output` but never reaches that copy, so an entry that\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448467182,"data":"   may outlive its timeout writes its record to an absolute path under\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44851895,"data":"   `/kaggle/working/output` and rewrites it after every finished unit of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44852963,"data":"   work, as `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py` does per row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448533885,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448538003,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448548307,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448551228,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448553723,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44856596,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448568669,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44857148,"data":"| cuquantum-cu11 | 24.8.0 (brings custatevec-cu11 1.6.0.post1 and cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0; the libraries the cu11 Aer wheel links) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448574277,"data":"| cutensor-cu11 | 2.2.0 (the newest release inside cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0's `\u003e=2.0.1,\u003c3`) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448577452,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448580159,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44858309,"data":"| quaternionic, clifford, kingdon, galgebra, pyoctonion | 1.0.18, 1.5.1, 3.0.0, 0.6.0, 3.12 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448585925,"data":"| pyquaternion | 0.9.9 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe (writes the VERSION.txt the sdist omits) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448588617,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448591275,"data":"| hyprat | 0.2.0 | GitHub tag archive, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448593897,"data":"| Octonion-Sedenion | 1.0.0 | PyPI wheel (its only release form), sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448596559,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI compiled wheel at the pin; `--extract` binds its Python files to the sha256-pinned sdist (Octonion-Sedenion builds on it) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448599367,"data":"| numba, sparse, anywidget | 0.68.0, 0.17.0, 0.11.0 | PyPI (`RUNTIME_PINS`; runtime dependencies of quaternionic, clifford and kingdon) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448602781,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448605497,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448608141,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448610578,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448613081,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448616397,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448619217,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.4486218,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448624363,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448630198,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448632864,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448635445,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.4486381,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448640608,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448643205,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448645747,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448648365,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448650943,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env` on a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448653583,"data":"  CPU or GPU machine, using CPU Aer either way. The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448656279,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448658879,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448661625,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448664027,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448666551,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448668958,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448671558,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448674139,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2, cuquantum-cu11 24.8.0 and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44867679,"data":"  cutensor-cu11 2.2.0 and sets `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448679376,"data":"- **cuStateVec.** `noise_simulator(..., custatevec=True)`, or\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448681991,"data":"  `GOROROBA_AER_CUSTATEVEC=1` in the entry's environment, sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448684586,"data":"  `cuStateVec_enable` on a GPU statevector or density-matrix run; `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448687271,"data":"  --workloads n21 --configurations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448689897,"data":"  cpu_statevector,gpu_statevector_unbatched,gpu_statevector_custatevec` records\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448692547,"data":"  the three paths with Aer's reported `cuStateVec_enable`. The option excludes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448695154,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`. `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` holds the library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448697779,"data":"  chain, the T4 push command and how to read its result.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448700371,"data":"- **Pinned GPU environment.** A push with `--gpu-env` runs the entry in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448703,"data":"  /tmp/gororoba/gpu-venv:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448705883,"data":"  - The venv runs the image's Python with the repository's pins and the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448708537,"data":"    Aer wheels in qiskit-aer's place.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44871108,"data":"  - Before the entry, gpu_env.json records each pin's installed version, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448716611,"data":"    owners of `qiskit_aer/__init__.py`, Aer's devices, and two seeded Bell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448719811,"data":"    runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448722322,"data":"  - A nonempty `failures` list stops the kernel with exit 4, before the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448724942,"data":"    entry starts. Each failure names what to fix:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448727551,"data":"    - a pin that resolved to another version;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448730128,"data":"    - a CPU qiskit-aer that shares the qiskit_aer/ files;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448732739,"data":"    - a GPU that nvidia-smi does not list;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448735299,"data":"    - a Bell run that raised, ran on another device, or left cuStateVec off.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448737945,"data":"  - Read gpu-env-report.txt and install-pins.txt in the output for the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448740628,"data":"    commands' own output.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448743135,"data":"  - \"Keeping the run on the GPU\" in `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` maps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.4487459,"data":"    each route to the CPU to the check that closes it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448748485,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448751035,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448753639,"data":"  method=...)`. On a GPU the simulator batches shots of circuits of at most\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44875624,"data":"  10 active qubits without control flow and runs feed-forward circuits shot\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448758849,"data":"  by shot (`calibration_snapshot.SnapshotSimulator`).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448761419,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448764005,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.4487666,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448769192,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448771765,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448774359,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448776932,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448779531,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448782113,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448784731,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44878732,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448789934,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448792742,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448795402000002,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448805969,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448808607,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.448811239,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.44881388,"data":"\n"}
